    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Charming period residence dating from circa 1903, originally owned by the local schoolmaster, set on a beautifully maintained site extending to approximately 0.3 acres. \n\nIdeally located just a short drive from Ballaghaderreen and its full range of amenities to include national & secondary schools, shops, restaurants, service providers, sporting facilities, etc, while also enjoying close proximity to Lough Gara and the village of Monasteraden.\n\nThoughtfully renovated and well maintained over the years, this delightful home retains a wealth of original character and period features, seamlessly complemented by modern comforts.\n\nAccommodation comprises of: \nGround Floor: \nWelcoming entrance hall featuring original stone flag flooring, \nCosy sitting room with an impressive stone wall and open fireplace, \nFully fitted and tiled kitchen/dining area with adjoining storage room,\nLiving room, complete with a feature stone wall, fireplace, and solid-fuel stove with back boiler.\nBathroom with separate shower unit \nFirst Floor: \n3 double bedrooms and a fully tiled shower room, enhanced by wood flooring and a timber ceiling.\n\nOriginal features include:\n•Wall panelling\n•Timber flooring\n•Original stone flag floor in the hallway\n\nExternally, the property enjoys a spacious side garden, offering a lovely outdoor setting, together with two useful rear sheds providing additional storage.\n\nHeating is provided by oil-fired central heating, complemented by a solid-fuel stove with back boiler, ensuring a comfortable and inviting home throughout the seasons.\n\nThis charming property offers a wonderful opportunity to acquire a character-filled period home in a peaceful yet convenient location, combining traditional features with practical modern living. \n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended.\n"
      },
